  "checks": [
    "InventoryGrid drag, drop and tooltip closures are held by the native widget. Each active dispatch retains a reference. Legacy C setters retire matching owned registrations, and Context destruction drops the final registration.",
    "Injected allocation failure retains the previous tooltip provider. UTF-8 clipping, invalidation after self-removal, expiry of the callback slot and checked exception delivery are exercised through the event queue.",
    "Input exercises accepted and rejected drops, drop self-removal, exception propagation after capture cleanup, and shrinking the grid during drag.",
    "Generated calls reach the three owned C setters directly. The hosted and static applications run identical callback tests. Only the hosted binary imports the XGE3 host library.",
    "The example renders in native graphics windows in Windows and Linux Xvfb. Input and tooltip edge cases are checked by the separate deterministic CPU fixture."
  ],
  "costs": [
    "Registration uses the existing native callback directory and associated language environment. Dispatch holds and drops the selected owner around the call. Drag and drop carry scalar payloads plus a callback-epoch widget view.",
    "Managed tooltip callbacks take one fixed-size native slot snapshot per invocation for resize safety. Any requested slot text becomes an owned language string. A returned tooltip is copied into the fixed native buffer up to 255 UTF-8 bytes and released.",
    "The profile compares recorded XRT allocations, frees and reallocations across 100 warmed accepted gestures with two scalar callbacks each. It validates exact callback counts for both native C and xlang. Setup, tooltip copies and event latency are outside this measurement."
  ],
  "pending": [
    "InventoryGrid managed slot icon/animation ownership, scroll model access, and slot render/animation-render callbacks.",
    "Whole-goal XGE, XUI and Document audit and matched release/IDE delivery."
  ],
